[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4289476651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118804#issuecomment-4289476651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118804","id":4289476651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_rDgr","user":{"login":"WSQS","id":17792626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzkyNjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17792626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS","html_url":"https://github.com/WSQS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T14:48:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T14:48:23Z","body":"> I don't think this is the correct way to fix this? You create an unnecessary color object, just to handle the earlier if statements checking for its existence. It might be a better idea to fix these if statements instead.\r\n\r\nMy concern with changing the existing early-return condition directly is that it is shared by multiple MSAA setup paths, while this bug only affects the internal-buffer path on GLES mobile/Web.\r\n\r\nSo I agree the real issue is in the setup check, but I don't think replacing the global condition outright is the safest fix. A better approach may be to make the completion check path-specific here, so the internal-buffer path no longer relies on `msaa3d.color`, without changing the behavior of the other MSAA paths.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4289476651/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4310000340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118804#issuecomment-4310000340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118804","id":4310000340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAOVi1A","user":{"login":"WSQS","id":17792626,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzkyNjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17792626?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS","html_url":"https://github.com/WSQS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WSQS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-24T02:16:36Z","updated_at":"2026-04-24T02:16:36Z","body":"@blueskythlikesclouds The main issue in upstream is that enabling glow on Android causes a rapid memory leak, which can lead to an OOM crash within minutes.\r\nIt seems that the correct fix is to make sure the lifetime of `msaa3d.fbo` stays aligned with `internal3d`. Since the Android internal-buffer MSAA path attaches `internal3d` textures to `msaa3d.fbo`, we probably need an additional check in `_clear_intermediate_buffers()` to invalidate or clear `msaa3d.fbo` when those intermediate buffers are freed.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4310000340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6314388552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118804#issuecomment-6314388552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118804","id":6314388552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABeF3sSA","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T11:05:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T11:05:09Z","body":"@WSQS it would be good if  you could test my fix and see if it resolves your issue. Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6314388552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"